    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Treat congestion with furosemide and start empagliflozin for HFpEF; move to as-needed furosemide guided by daily weights once euvolemic. Guideline: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); 2023 ACC Expert Consensus Decision Pathway on Management of Heart Failure With Preserved Ejection Fraction (2023) [S]</item><item>Add low-dose spironolactone for HFpEF with blood pressure above target once potassium and kidney function are stable. Guideline: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); 2023 ACC Expert Consensus Decision Pathway on Management of Heart Failure With Preserved Ejection Fraction (2023) [S]</item><item>Cardiology referral to confirm the diagnosis, review the echocardiogram, and look for specific causes such as amyloidosis or valve disease. Guideline: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); 2023 ACC Expert Consensus Decision Pathway on Management of Heart Failure With Preserved Ejection Fraction (2023) [S]</item><item>Check a basic metabolic panel and magnesium one to two weeks after starting or changing diuretic, SGLT2 inhibitor, or mineralocorticoid antagonist therapy, then every three to six months; KCCQ-12 every three to six months. Guideline: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, heart failure monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Daily weights, sodium moderation, a written travel plan for weight gain, and continued daily walking; refer to cardiac rehabilitation if exercise tolerance plateaus. Guideline: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, heart failure monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Pneumococcal and RSV vaccination and a yearly high-dose influenza vaccine to lower the risk of respiratory infection in heart failure. Guideline: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, heart failure monograph (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
